            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Brownie1"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I boil 3 cinnamon sticks in 3 cups water. Let it cool. Then put cinnamon water in blender w/1 can evap milk, 1 can condensed milk, 1 can coconut milk and 1 tsp vanilla extract and Rum(I use Malibu Rum/coconut flavor). NO EGGS. Serve on the rocks and garnish w/ground cinnamon. Yummy!!!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent! Everyone loves it on Christmas Day. Made a few changes from reviews read. Used 3 cups of cinnamon water, 1 can cream of coconut, 1 can coconut milk, 1 can evaporated milk and 1 can sweetened condensed milk. Added ground cloves, nutmeg and 1 tsp vanilla. Mixed with 2 cups rum. Refrigerated for 1-2 days and served cold. Big hit for our Holiday event. Not a drop left so I'm making another batch for our New Years celebration.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-26T23:57:47.853Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Eric"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is real traditional puerto rican coquito from my childhood, the best one, simple and very good.\nI added 1/3 cup sugar for my taste.\nTraditional coquito don't has eggs, if you add eggs then you are making eggnog that is a different drink.",
            "datePublished": "2020-11-27T00:26:59.367Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
